Licenses for the fonts Trimpod ships. English mode uses the original ChicagoFLF
files unchanged. Russian mode uses Mulmaru for every available UI glyph,
including Latin, digits, punctuation, symbols and Cyrillic. PixelMplus fills
missing Japanese glyphs, and Schumacher Clean is the fallback system font
compiled into the binary.

----- ChicagoFLF (unchanged English UI .fnt files) -----

ChicagoFLF by Robin Casady, a reproduction of Susan Kare's Chicago.
Released by the author into the public domain.

----- PixelMplus (fallback Japanese glyphs in the Russian UI family) -----

The Japanese (kana/kanji/fullwidth) glyphs in the .fnt files are rasterized
from PixelMplus12-Regular by Itou Hiroki (https://github.com/itouhiro/PixelMplus),
a pixel-style outline conversion of the M+ bitmap fonts.
Copyright (C) 2013 M+ Font Project.  Distributed under the M+ FONT LICENSE:

M+ FONTS                                Copyright (C) 2002-2013 M+ FONTS PROJECT

These fonts are free software.
Unlimited permission is granted to use, copy, and distribute them, with
or without modification, either commercially or noncommercially.
THESE FONTS ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTY.

http://mplus-fonts.sourceforge.jp/mplus-outline-fonts/

----- Mulmaru (complete Russian UI family) -----

Copyright (c) 2025, Mushsooni (https://github.com/mushsooni/mulmaru),
with Reserved Font Name "Mulmaru" and "Mulmaru Mono".

Distributed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. The unmodified
Mulmaru.ttf source and the complete license are included under fonts/sources.
The modified derivative is named TrimpodRus in accordance with the Reserved
Font Name requirement. It adds one blank logical pixel after each visible glyph
to improve Russian UI readability.

